# The limits `regatta limit` changes live (modules/regatta/libexec/limit; live-limits, 2026-11-01): see wharf-runs'
# `limits` for the columns. Account limits come in soft/hard pairs (`<login>:<pct>`, `*:` for any login that sets no own
# rule in `accounts.json` or `budgets.json`), read by `bin/account` over `budgets.json` and `accounts.json` on that host
# (account-limit-pairs, 2026-11-07).
lighthouse/week-soft-max  login  -  bin/account limit-read week-soft-max {login}
lighthouse/week-hard-max  login  -  bin/account limit-read week-hard-max {login}
lighthouse/week-finish-hard-max  login  -  bin/account limit-read week-finish-hard-max {login}
lighthouse/window-soft-max  login  -  bin/account limit-read window-soft-max {login}
lighthouse/window-hard-max  login  -  bin/account limit-read window-hard-max {login}
# Old live keys kept reading as aliases until every host has the pair keys (`week-max`: own line hard, `*:` soft).
# alias: lighthouse/week-soft-max (*:) and lighthouse/week-hard-max (LOGIN:)
lighthouse/week-max  login  -  bin/account week-max {login}
# alias: lighthouse/week-finish-hard-max
lighthouse/week-max-finish  login  -  bin/account week-max {login} --for finish
# alias: lighthouse/week-hard-max
lighthouse/overdraw-max  login  -  bin/account week-max {login} --for overdraw
# reef's bounds (bin/reef; 2026-11-04): `mode=on|advise|off,run=<floor>-<ceiling>,check=<floor>-<ceiling>` per host,
# a `*:` line (a host without its own) only in the base file, as `regatta limit set` takes `<host>:` or `--all`; within
# them reef moves wharf-runs' run-cap and check-slots by the host's load.
lighthouse/reef  host*  mode=advise  REEF_HOST={host} bin/reef bounds
